implementationPlan.description:
Drift (b), ps1 only: the infra-failure CheckRun for an interrupted worktree-mode gate. Test first, then fix.

sh's EXIT trap calls finish_gate_observation (about sh:5918). For a gate that started and was never recorded, that stops the child and records outcome infra-failure against FROZEN_CANDIDATE_ID/FROZEN_TREE. ps1 does this only in the shared Invoke-MoeLanding finally (about ps1:6250-6262).

In worktree mode, the gate runs inside Invoke-MoeWorktreeRounds (about ps1:6991-6997) on a LOCAL $frozen:
- the outer finally only calls Stop-MoeGateChild (about ps1:11222);
- $script:MoeFrozen is null in worktree mode, so neither the outer finally nor Invoke-MoeWorktreeCompletion's finally has a candidate to record against.

TEST. Add `async function wtGateInterrupt()` to step 2's block, and add it to step 2's registration line:
- p=repo('wt-gate-interrupt',{settings:{...LANDS,qualityGate:gateCmd()}}), main=mainOf(p), log=path.join(root,'wt-gate-interrupt-gate.jsonl').
- r=landRun(p,'wt-gate-interrupt',{'src/a.txt':'done\n'},{...REVIEW,WT_GATE_LOG:log,WT_GATE_SLEEP_MS:'60000'},{ready:log}).
  - The gate appends to its log as it starts, so the barrier falls mid-gate.
  - sh gets a SIGTERM; ps1 gets one real Ctrl+C on its own console (consoleSupervisor).
  - The ps1 gate child runs on its own console (CREATE_NO_WINDOW), so only the wrapper is interrupted.
- t=revOf(p.top,p.branch); M=git(p.top,'merge-tree','--write-tree','refs/heads/main',t).trim(); cand=rpcs(p).filter(x=>x.tool==='record_candidate'); runs=rpcs(p).filter(x=>x.tool==='record_check_run').
- Assert, each with tail(r.log):
  - present(log+'.sent') && !ended(p): the session was cut short, as wtTeardown checks;
  - rows(log).length===1;
  - runs.map(x=>[x.args.outcome,x.args.candidateId,x.args.treeSha]) deep-equals [['infra-failure',cand[0].args.id,M]];
  - mainOf(p)===main, `git show t:src/a.txt` is 'done\n', and no journal(p);
  - finals(p) deep-equals [['failed',undefined]] and phase(p)==='closed' (design §2.6, as wtTeardown's 'pre' row);
  - leased(p,r,1): the check run comes before the one release, and the release before deregister_worker.

Run `MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-gate-interrupt`. ps1 must FAIL (RED: no record_check_run). sh must pass, because its EXIT trap already records the run.

FIX (ps1, Invoke-MoeWorktreeRounds' gate block only):
```
$frozen = $null; $gated = $false
try {
    try { $frozen = New-MoeFrozenCandidate $Git $m $b } catch {}
    $gated = $frozen -and (Send-MoeCandidate ...) -and (Invoke-MoeFrozenGate ... -WorktreeMode)
} finally { <twin of finish_gate_observation> }
if (-not $gated) { <the existing MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE lines, unchanged> }
```
The finally runs only when $frozen, $script:MoeGate and $script:MoeGate.Started are all set and $script:MoeGate.Recorded is not. It then, in order:
1. calls Stop-MoeGateChild in its own try/catch, warning '[WARN] Cannot stop owned qualityGate process: ...' as Remove-MoeGateWorkspace does;
2. sets Recorded=$true and Outcome='infra-failure';
3. runs `Send-MoeCheckRun $frozen $script:MoeGate | Out-Null` inside try/catch, with a [WARN] that names the failure.
Comment: 'Twin: finish_gate_observation. An interrupted gate was never verified: no pass, whatever its exit code.'

Why here and not in the completion's finally or the outer finally (the description offers both):
- the candidate is already in scope;
- the record lands before any unlanded-route RPC or finalize, on every path: a Ctrl+C, or a throw between Started and Recorded;
- the lease release in Invoke-MoeWorktreeCompletion's finally still comes after it, as in sh;
- it stays out of Invoke-MoeWorktreeCompletion, which task-f9874361 edits.

Untouched: shared mode (Invoke-MoeLanding, Invoke-MoeFrozenGate) and the migration (its -NoEvidence sets Recorded at the start). Do not attach anything to Console.CancelKeyPress (mem:gotcha-wrapper-clean-gate-shutdown). See also mem:gotcha-wrapper-teardown-finalize-parity and mem:decision-worktree-gate-arm-contract.

Error handling: a failed stop or record only warns and never changes the landing outcome. The outer finally's Stop-MoeGateChild and Remove-MoeGateWorkspace still clean up.

After the fix: run ParseFile on PS 5.1, and keep moe-agent.ps1 as UTF-8 with its BOM. Re-run wt-gate-interrupt on ps1 and sh: both must pass (GREEN).

Drift (d), both twins: MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT at the landing post-flight. Test first, then fix.

Design §1.6 (docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md:69) says: "A post-flight that finds it still lands ... and prints the code". Today only the pre-flight guard, the removal and the sweep print MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT.

TEST. Add `async function wtMoePost()` to step 2's block and its registration line:
- p=repo('wt-moe-post',{settings:LANDS}), main=mainOf(p), plus a regex for the code line: `\[WARN\] MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT: .*\.moe exists; no commit carries \.moe \(DENY\)`.
- Checkpoint: r=landRun(p,'wt-moe-post-1',{'src/a.txt':'one\n','.moe/x':'x\n'}). The fake CLI writes W/.moe during the session, after the pre-flight guard. Assert:
  - r.log has exactly one code line;
  - t=revOf(p.top,p.branch) has parents [main];
  - `git diff --name-only main t` is exactly src/a.txt;
  - W/.moe/x still reads 'x\n'.
- Then fs.rmSync(path.join(p.W,'.moe'),{recursive:true,force:true}), so the next pre-flight passes its guard.
- Completion: r=landRun(p,'wt-moe-post-2',{'src/a.txt':'two\n','.moe/y':'y\n'},REVIEW) and c=mainOf(p). Assert:
  - exactly one code line;
  - parents(p.top,c) is [main];
  - `git diff --name-only main c` is exactly src/a.txt, and `git show c:src/a.txt` is 'two\n';
  - the last done(p) row is committed with sha c;
  - W/.moe/y still reads 'y\n'.
- The fixture's main tracks .moe/ files, so check that .moe is unchanged by diff; never assert that C's tree has no .moe.

Run `MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-moe-post`: it must FAIL on both engines (RED).

FIX (both twins, one check each, at the top of the worktree worker post-flight, before any landing):
- sh: in worktree_postflight, right after `MOE_WT_COMPLETION="$completion"`.
- ps1: in Invoke-MoeWorktreePostflight, right after `$script:MoeWtCompletion = $completion`.
Presence test:
- sh: `[ -e "$MOE_WT_PATH/.moe" ] || [ -L "$MOE_WT_PATH/.moe" ]`.
- ps1: `Get-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $script:MoeWtPath '.moe') -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` is non-null. Like sh's -L, this sees a dangling link; the removal guard at about ps1:7760 uses the same test.
- Both skip the check when the W path is empty.
Print ONE line, the same sentence in both twins:
`[WARN] MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT: <W>/.moe exists; no commit carries .moe (DENY), and the next pre-flight stops the seat for a human to inspect it.`
- sh: `echo -e "${YELLOW}[WARN]${NC} MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT: $MOE_WT_PATH/.moe exists; ..."`.
- ps1: `Write-Host "[WARN] MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT: $($script:MoeWtPath)/.moe exists; ..." -ForegroundColor Yellow`.
Keep the sentence a whole literal in each twin (mem:gotcha-parity-check-literals).

Nothing else changes:
- the landing runs exactly as before: DENY keeps .moe/** out of W's commits, and L5's board guard checks M;
- no RPC, comment or report_blocked is added;
- W/.moe is never deleted;
- the control-seat post-flight is untouched.

Error handling: the check only reads the file system and cannot fail the post-flight.

After the fix:
1. `bash -n` and ParseFile;
2. re-run wt-moe-post on sh and ps1: both must pass (GREEN);
3. run the codes case (MOE_WORKTREE_ code-family parity) on sh;
4. run `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh`.
